NAME
       wait, waitpid - wait for a child to change state

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/wait.h>

       pid_t wait(int *status);
       pid_t waitpid(pid_t pid, int *status, int options);

DESCRIPTION
       Blocks until a child exits and reports which one. PID may name a
       single child, or -1 for any.

       WNOHANG in OPTIONS makes the call return 0 at once when no child
       has exited, which is the way to poll a child while doing
       something else, such as drawing a progress bar for a long
       operation running in a forked helper.

       STATUS is inspected with WIFEXITED and WEXITSTATUS.

RETURN VALUE
       The pid of the child, 0 for WNOHANG with nothing ready, or -1
       with errno set.

ERRORS
       ECHILD   the caller has no such child
       EINTR    a signal arrived first

EXAMPLE
              pid_t p = fork();
              if (p == 0) { work(); _exit(0); }
              for (;;) {
                      if (waitpid(p, &st, WNOHANG) == p) break;
                      draw_progress();
                      usleep(150000);
              }

SEE ALSO
       fork(2), exit(2), execve(2)
